<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Welfesholz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1115">1115</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Welfesholz was fought on 11 February 1115 in the Mansfeld area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> princes led by Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Lothair of Supplinburg</a> defeated the army of Emperor Henry V, whose efforts to extend royal power and lands in Saxony had provoked revolt. The defeat ended effective Salian authority in Saxony and strengthened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a>, who was elected king in 1125.</p></div>
